"""
TKDL-01b — REAL sample TKDL records, extracted from actual saved TKDL portal
pages (the 21 HTML files the team captured from tkdl.res.in's public demo
search results, saved as web-archive HTML).

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS SEPARATELY FROM tkdl_mock_records.py:
That file's 6 hand-curated records were written to hit specific demo beats
(exact scenario matches, ingredient-category spread). These 21 are different:
they are UNEDITED IN SUBSTANCE — same record IDs, ingredients, "knowledge
known since" figures, and classical-text citations as the real saved pages —
only reformatted into this project's TKDLRecord/TKDLIngredient schema.

MOCK VS REAL, PER PROJECT INSTRUCTIONS SECTION 28 — READ THIS BEFORE DEMOING:
  - The DATA is real: these are actual TKDL prior-art records, not invented.
  - The MODULE remains "mock" / "demo": there is still no live query against
    tkdl.res.in. This is a static offline capture, exactly like
    tkdl_mock_records.py, and every record still carries is_mock=True.
  - Say, if asked: "TKDL Search — DEMO / MOCK, built on real saved TKDL
    prior-art records" — never "connected to TKDL" or "live TKDL".

KNOWN DATA-QUALITY CAVEATS (small, and worth stating plainly rather than
hiding — consistent with the project's abstention/no-fake-precision stance):
  1. TRANSLITERATION: the source pages render Sanskrit titles through a
     custom display font (SHREE-DIA-1900), which decodes to mangled glyphs
     under normal text encodings. formulation_name below is a best-effort
     ASCII transliteration (diacritics dropped, e.g. "Bhringaraja Tailam"),
     cross-checked against known classical formulation names. One title
     (TKDL-HG-509) has a single glyph the team could not confidently resolve
     — flagged inline. If a judge or reviewer questions exact Sanskrit
     spelling, say so plainly and offer to show the original saved HTML page.
  2. INGREDIENT SOURCE_CATEGORY: TKDL's own pages don't label ingredients as
     plant/animal/mineral — that's this project's classification, applied
     here by a simple rule (botanical Latin-binomial pattern -> plant; a
     short hand-checked list of minerals/metals and animal-derived items ->
     mineral/animal). A handful of composite classical groupings (e.g.
     "dashamula" = ten roots, "panchalavana" = five salts) are hardcoded.
     This is the SAME heuristic-classification approach already used for
     the 6 records in tkdl_mock_records.py, just applied at larger scale.
  3. therapeutic_use lists are trimmed to the first several well-formed
     entries per record where the source page's sentence structure parsed
     cleanly; a few longer/garbled fragments were dropped rather than risk
     a misleading entry (again: abstain over guess).

INTEGRATION: nothing else needs to change to use this. tkdl_mock_records.py
imports TKDL_REAL_RECORDS from here and concatenates it onto the existing
6-record list — backend/logic/tkdl_search.py iterates TKDL_MOCK_RECORDS
generically and needs no changes at all.
"""

